cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: >-
  If you use LVec in research, please cite the software and record the exact
  release version or Git commit used, along with the relevant dependencies.
title: 'LVec: Lorentz and spatial vectors for physics analysis'
version: 0.3.3
authors:
  - family-names: Elashri
    given-names: Mohamed
repository-code: 'https://github.com/MohamedElashri/lvec'
repository-artifact: 'https://pypi.org/project/lvec/'
url: 'https://github.com/MohamedElashri/lvec'
abstract: >-
  LVec provides Lorentz four-vectors and spatial vectors for physics analysis
  with NumPy and optional Awkward Array backends. It includes reference-frame
  transformations, event reductions, angular observables, cached properties,
  and selective numerical precision recovery.
keywords:
  - physics
  - Lorentz vectors
  - relativistic kinematics
  - NumPy
  - Awkward Array
